CommitDate: Tue Nov 3 16:05:45 2026 -0500

    board: file CF-128 + CF-129 — an ancestry leg no fixture can red, and a documented --repo form the tool reds. Addresses CF-128, CF-129.
    
    CF-128 (P3): tests/selftest.sh section 29 runs seven fixtures and every one passes
    --published-dir, which short-circuits the Git read and the HEAD-ancestry leg at
    scripts/board_drift.py:165. Deleting that leg leaves the suite at SELFTEST: PASS with all 7
    publish-drift arms green, while the unmodified tool still prints `FAIL  HEAD ancestry` on a
    divergent fixture — AGENTS.md rule 2 (every check needs a fixture that proves its failure
    path) is unmet for the one leg docs/BOARD.md's PASS definition depends on.
    
    CF-129 (P4): docs/BOARD.md:54 says --repo selects the repository resolving the ref, but the
    ancestry leg resolves --ref in the workdir (:167-172), so the documented reviewer form prints
    `FAIL  HEAD ancestry — git rev-parse --verify pub^{commit}: exit 128` and RESULT: DRIFT
    against identical board bytes, and only --no-head turns it green.
    
    Filed from a throwaway clone of origin/main (family barrier: sibling lanes were running on the
    shared checkout, one of them mid-`tests/selftest.sh`). The shared checkout was never read as a
    write target, never cleaned, and never touched. Guard position disclosed: a fresh clone
    carries no installed Git hooks and this host sets no core.hooksPath, so no hook ran on this
    commit — the configured checks were run manually at this tree (`bash tests/selftest.sh` ->
    SELFTEST: PASS; `bash scripts/boardctl validate` -> RESULT: OK (44 warnings)) and the GitReins
    Tier-2 judge on CF-128-QA1 is the gate for the filing.
    
    Drafted as CF-125/CF-126; renumbered to CF-128/CF-129 at append time because a sibling lane
    consumed those ids in 8df6b38 (README Quick-start dogfood walk, unrelated subject).
